      "original_statement": "For an object whose Hom functor preserves all countable sums, maps to a sequential homotopy colimit form the colimit of the stage Hom groups.",
      "proved_statement": "For any object P and this sequence, write A_r for the direct sum of stage Hom groups, B_r=Hom(P,S[r]), Q_r=B_r/A_r, d_r induced by u[r] and e_r its quotient map. The comparison kernel is coker(ker d_0 to ker e_0), and its cokernel lies in the exact sequence 0 to coker e_0 to coker lambda to ker d_1 to 0. These give the exact bijectivity criterion and weaker sufficient conditions.",
      "hypotheses": "Only a triangulated category, the particular countable coproduct S, and its defining telescope triangle; r=0,1.",
      "proof": {
        "file": "PROOFS_10139_10427.md",
        "bytes": 19208,
        "sha256": "64232DDDE5300956C056880DBDA2E3E777477C2FAA7EAE9545261657A23C50C5",
        "section": 7
      },
      "status": "proved_editorial_consequence",
      "body_replacement": false,
      "novelty": "not_claimed",
      "example": "Every constant identity sequence satisfies the criterion for every P, including the noncompact countable direct sum of Z[0] in D(Ab); the exact splitting and quotient inverse are constructed.",
      "limits": "This is a statement for a specified object and sequence. It does not infer that P is compact or that arbitrary homotopy colimits are functorial."
    }
  ],
